{"`open(url)` uses `Kernel#open`, which follows arbitrary URLs and can execute shell commands (strings starting with `|`). This enables SSRF against internal services and potential RCE. Use a dedicated HTTP library or OpenURI with URI validation and validate the URL against an allow-list of external hosts before fetching.": 0.971656084060669, "Insecure origin validation: `indexOf` performs a substring match, so any origin that is a prefix of `discourseUrl` will pass. An attacker origin `https://forum.example.co` would bypass the check when `discourseUrl` is `https://forum.example.com/`.": 0.8342922329902649, "`contents` is used without a nil guard (`<<` will raise `NoMethodError` if nil), and `url` is interpolated directly into an HTML anchor tag without escaping. A crafted URL can inject arbitrary HTML/JS, leading to stored XSS.": 0.9912741780281067, "`end if` is a syntax error - it's missing a condition. This should be `end` to close the `if/else` block. As written, this template will fail to render.": 0.8933947086334229, "`force: true` on `create_table` in a migration will silently drop the `top_topics` table and all its data if it already exists. This risks production data loss if the migration is ever re-run.": 0.9158859848976135, "Unbounded reload loop: `document.location.reload()` fires every 30 seconds with no retry limit or backoff. If the embed content never becomes available, each visitor's browser will hammer the server indefinitely.": 0.8844925761222839, "`force: true` on `create_table` in migration will silently drop and recreate the `topic_embeds` table if it already exists, destroying all data.": 0.9064714908599854, "XSS / incorrect escaping: `request.referer` is output with HTML escaping inside a JavaScript string context. HTML escaping corrupts URLs containing `&` and is not the correct defense against JavaScript injection. Use `escape_javascript` for JS string contexts.": 0.9826011061668396, "Using `raw` to render `post.cooked` in an embed view risks XSS on the embedding site if server-side sanitization is ever bypassed. Consider wrapping in an additional sanitize pass.": 0.5391415357589722, "`import_remote` fetches each thread URL live via `open(url).read` with no error handling. If any Disqus thread URL is unreachable, the entire import will abort with an unhandled exception.": 0.9685924053192139, "`TopicEmbed.import_remote` does not accept or forward a `created_at` parameter, so the original Disqus thread timestamps are silently discarded. All imported topics will be dated as of the import time.": 0.9039605855941772, "Early return bypasses the `:after_post_cook` plugin filter. Plugins that register filters on cooked content will silently skip `raw_html` posts.": 0.7582019567489624, "Race condition: `setnx` + `expire` is not atomic. If the process dies between the two calls, the key persists with no TTL, permanently blocking retrieval for this embed URL.": 0.9959602952003479, "The return value of `@post.save(...)` is not checked. If validation fails, subsequent operations still execute on an unsaved post, and `revise!` returns `true`.": 0.9257729053497314, "Wrong file required in spec. This loads `ProcessPost` instead of `PollFeed`. Should be `require 'jobs/scheduled/poll_feed'`.": 0.8904464244842529, "`i.content` can be nil for RSS items that lack a `content` element. Calling `.scrub` on nil will raise `NoMethodError`, crashing the job.": 0.9985207915306091, "The `embed_url` parameter is used without URL format validation. It's eventually fetched by `TopicRetriever` which calls `open(url).read`. Without verifying the URL scheme is `http`/`https` and the host is not an internal address, this is an SSRF vector.": 0.9895685315132141, "Add rel=\"noopener\" to target=\"_blank\" links to prevent opener access.": 0.1949724406003952, "Assertions in `after` block is an anti-pattern. If an example raises before reaching `get :best`, the `after` block still runs and fails on the response check, masking the real error.": 0.38555672764778137, "No null check on `comments`. If the `#discourse-comments` element is absent from the page, `comments.appendChild(iframe)` will throw a `TypeError`.": 0.916205108165741, "`start_with?(...).should be_true` is a weak assertion that hides both partial matches and diff details on failure. Use `should ==` for an exact comparison.": 0.3744940161705017, "Test passes for the wrong reason. `feed_polling_enabled?` is not stubbed to `true`, so the AND condition short-circuits before `feed_polling_url` is ever evaluated.": 0.991367757320404, "Same issue: `feed_polling_enabled?` and `feed_polling_url` are not stubbed to truthy values, so test passes because earlier AND conditions fail.": 0.9709723591804504, "`feed_key` is defined but never called - this is dead code.": 0.7652694582939148, "Spec expects `TopicRetriever` to be called, but the controller enqueues `Jobs.enqueue(:retrieve_topic, ...)` instead.": 0.9482332468032837, "`ALLOWALL` is not a valid `X-Frame-Options` value per RFC 7034. Some browsers treat unrecognized values as `DENY`, which would prevent the embed from loading.": 0.9154381155967712, "Guard against a nil/empty RSS parse result before iterating to avoid a NoMethodError when the feed fails to parse.": 0.8136448264122009, "Guard against a blank referrer before calling postMessage; an empty targetOrigin will throw and break the resize messaging.": 0.8461964726448059, "Missing newline at end of file in embed.css.scss.": 0.2678211033344269}